# RISK-09 hooks are shell scripts and this repo has core.autocrlf=true with no
# repo-wide .gitattributes, so a checkout would otherwise write them with CRLF.
#
# Measured 31 Aug 2026: a CRLF hook still fires under Git for Windows - the
# bundled sh tolerates the carriage return. This line is portability insurance,
# not a fix for an observed break here. On Linux and macOS a shebang ending in
# CR fails with "bad interpreter", which would leave a guard that is present,
# executable and does nothing. Not verified on this machine.
* text eol=lf
